A freedive on Kirra Reef, straight out off the beach at Coolangatta. Clean blue water for once, looked like 8 to 10m of visibility, with a bit of surf on the way out and the reef shallow enough to work comfortably on a breath. Sponge-covered bommies with baitfish stacked over the top the whole session, a pair of pineapple fish tucked up under a ledge and a spotted wobbegong lying out on the reef late on. Both are tagged on screen as they appear.

## Dive stats

- **Location:** Kirra Reef, QLD
- **Date:** 4 July 2026
- **Depth:** 4.6m avg, 8.1m max
- **Visibility:** 8-10m

## Highlights

Pineapple Fish and Spotted Wobbegong
